nyciml-2025-26-spring-juniora-10.body:
Let $a_n$ be the number of tilings of $2\times n$; $a_0 = a_1 = 1$. Look at the left column:
- a vertical domino: $a_{n-1}$ ways;
- two horizontal dominoes or a $2\times 2$ block: $a_{n-2}$ ways each;
- an L-block covering the left column and one cell of column 2 ($2$ orientations). Then horizontal dominoes are forced in a staggered strip until a second L-block closes off a straight edge, leaving $a_{n-3}, a_{n-4}, \dots, a_0$ ways.

So $a_n = a_{n-1} + 2a_{n-2} + 2(a_{n-3} + \dots + a_0)$, which simplifies to $a_{n+1} = 2a_n + a_{n-1}$. Hence $a_0, \dots, a_6 = 1, 1, 3, 7, 17, 41, 99$.

**Answer: $99$**
